    <node id="instruction">
      <data key="d0">instruction</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "instruction" refers to a command or set of directions designed to guide a user through a specific action or process. It encompasses various forms of guidance, including clicking menu items, buttons, links, or executing actions such as selecting categories like 'Electronics'. Instructions are often used to perform tasks or navigate interfaces, with examples ranging from simple clicks to more complex commands like searching for information. Essentially, an instruction is a directive that prompts a user to take a particular step towards achieving a goal or completing a task. Examples include clicking actions to select categories such as 'Beauty &amp; Personal Care', interacting with a link, or clicking a menu item like 'Sports &amp; Outdoors'. Additionally, instructions can involve navigating to specific pages, such as the sign-in page, or performing specific actions by clicking menu items, such as 'Beauty &amp; Personal Care'. An instruction typically provides guidance for interacting with a user interface element, and it can also be described as a set of directions or commands. Specific examples of instructions include clicking the menu item 'Tools &amp; Home Improvement', clicking a link, and clicking a menu item 'Video Games'.

In the context of this input, several instances of instructions are described, each involving the act of clicking different menu items or links. These examples include clicking the menu item 'Health &amp; Household', clicking a link, and clicking the menu item 'Office Products'. All of these instructions are part of a broader definition of an instruction as a command or set of directions designed to guide a user through a specific action or process.&lt;SEP&gt;An instruction to click a menu item&lt;SEP&gt;An instruction to click a link named 'My Wish List'.&lt;SEP&gt;An instruction to click a menu item.&lt;SEP&gt;An instruction to click a link</data>
