    <node id="role">
      <data key="d0">role</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "role" is versatile and can denote a specific assignment, function, or concept related to different elements or entities. In the context of a menu item, it signifies a specific assignment related to the item, such as an action associated with a menu item. Similarly, in the context of an element, it signifies a role or function associated with that element, like the role of a combobox or a role attribute. The term "menu item role" further specifies this concept, emphasizing its application within a menu structure. Additionally, "role or function" is a general descriptor that encompasses the idea of a role or function in a broader sense. Furthermore, "a concept representing the role of the button" and "a concept representing the role of a link" highlight how roles can be conceptualized in terms of buttons and links, respectively. Lastly, "a role or function associated with an element" and "a role indicating the element type" reiterate the notion that roles are often linked to elements and can indicate their type or function. The term "role" also has specific applications, such as accessibility roles, which are attributes used to describe the function of an element on a webpage. A role is a concept that can be assigned to various elements, including menu items, buttons, links, and other interface components, to define their function or purpose within the system. Roles are also associated with specific menu items, such as "Tools &amp; Home Improvement," "Video Games," and "Sports &amp; Outdoors." The role of a link element is specifically mentioned, indicating its importance in defining the function of a link within a system. A role assigned to the menu item 'Electronics' indicates its function within the menu structure, likely categorizing content related to electronics. The role of a link in a user interface signifies the action to perform when the link is clicked, directing the user to another page or resource. A role indicating the action to perform suggests that the element is designed to execute a specific task or command. Role of an element in a user interface denotes the function or purpose of the element within the interface, contributing to the overall usability and functionality of the system. The role of a web element, such as a menu or a link, is crucial for defining the function of the element on a webpage, ensuring that users can navigate and interact effectively with the content.&lt;SEP&gt;A role assigned to a menu item.&lt;SEP&gt;A role indicating the element is a link&lt;SEP&gt;The role of a link in a user interface&lt;SEP&gt;A role assigned to the combobox element.&lt;SEP&gt;A role assigned to a menu item&lt;SEP&gt;A role in a menu item</data>
