    <edge source="instruction" target="click">
      <data key="d7">122.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The term "click" refers to an action performed on a link or an element, such as a button or a checkbox. It is often associated with instructions that guide users on how to execute this action. For instance, an instruction might specify the need to click on a particular link or element to activate a combobox or trigger another action. These instructions can be part of a larger set of guidelines or user interface elements designed to facilitate user interaction. The relationship between a click and an instruction highlights the role of instructions in guiding users through various actions, ensuring that they understand how to interact with digital interfaces effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Instruction specifies action of clicking on an element&lt;SEP&gt;action&lt;SEP&gt;Action to perform on the element&lt;SEP&gt;Action of pressing&lt;SEP&gt;Action verb for hyperlink</data>
      <data key="d9">Action,Artifact,Position Product Name Price,action,action_for,click,is action,is related to,the link</data>
